<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Quickgrass — the engineered lawn. The pyrelands sheet's ruling
    (the_pyrelands.md §water answer, owner 2026-09-10): a Rakatan-engineered
    forage crop gone feral — roots driven to the water table by design,
    regrowth in days by design, dominance by design. The war left a lawn,
    still working as built. It is the "quickgrass sprints back" step of the
    ruled fire chain, and with the generic grasses evicted (owner card,
    2026-09-11: pyrelands ground layer = quickgrass + commissioned fire-chain
    flora only) it is the biome's forage base.

    Division of labour with EmberGrass.xml: ember grass is the FUEL —
    standing tinder, flammability 1.6, everything into height and nothing
    into water. Quickgrass is the FORAGE — taproot to the water table, so it
    comes back green onto warm ash and feeds the ash-grazers. It burns like
    an ordinary lawn (0.7), not like the fuel bed; the fire passes THROUGH
    it and it is back inside two days, which is the engineered point.

    growDays 0.5: "regrowth in days by design", faster even than ember grass
    (0.8) — the burn never outruns the lawn. Same lifespan trap as ember
    grass: lifespanDaysPerGrowDays 42 puts the lifespan back at a normal
    ~21 days.

    ⚠️ Same flagged-not-guessed tint assumption as EmberGrass.xml /
    ScorchFruit.xml: no vanilla plant sets graphicData <color>; if CutoutPlant
    ignores it the plant renders plain green — cosmetic only. The colour is
    the ruled flora accent, regrowth green #62c944.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_FE_Plant_Quickgrass</defName>
    <label>quickgrass</label>
    <description>A low, dense forage grass that comes back onto burned ground while the ash is still warm, green against the black inside a day or two. Its roots run absurdly deep for its size — down to the water table, in defiance of everything the surface suggests — and its blades carry more food than any wild grass has a right to. It was engineered that way, twenty-five millennia ago, by gardeners who wanted this ground to feed things. The gardeners are gone. The lawn is still working.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>85</MaxHitPoints>
      <!-- An ordinary lawn's burn, not the fuel bed's: the fire chain
           needs it back two days after the front passes, and it is the
           water-carrier of the pair. -->
      <Flammability>0.7</Flammability>
      <!-- Engineered forage: above ember grass (0.45) by design — this is
           what the ash-grazers and the Tribes' herds actually live on. -->
      <Nutrition>0.7</Nutrition>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/Grass</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <color>(98, 201, 68)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <hideAtSnowOrSandDepth>0.5</hideAtSnowOrSandDepth>
    <ingestible />
    <plant>
      <!-- The taproot is the fertility story: it grows on a fresh ash
           trace and a light bank exactly as ember grass does, and stops at
           the same heavy-ash rungs, so the ash ladder keeps its meaning. -->
      <fertilityMin>0.05</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.1</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>0.5</growDays>
      <lifespanDaysPerGrowDays>42</lifespanDaysPerGrowDays>
      <leaflessGraphicPath>Things/Plant/Grass_Leafless</leaflessGraphicPath>
      <harvestWork>40</harvestWork>
      <maxMeshCount>9</maxMeshCount>
      <visualSizeRange>0.4~0.7</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0.4</topWindExposure>
      <wildClusterRadius>5</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>18</wildClusterWeight>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <!-- Same engineered span as the rest of the kit: still growing on
           ground hot enough to scorch, unbothered by a night frost. -->
      <minGrowthTemperature>-4</minGrowthTemperature>
      <minOptimalGrowthTemperature>8</minOptimalGrowthTemperature>
      <maxOptimalGrowthTemperature>50</maxOptimalGrowthTemperature>
      <maxGrowthTemperature>80</maxGrowthTemperature>
      <growMinGlow>0.31</growMinGlow>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
